    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (78.84) and **Josh Lowe** (67.55). Both outfielders draw highly favorable matchups against Randy V\u00e1squez and Aaron Civale, respectively. **Kyle Tucker**\u2019s elite SP Skill projection (+19%) and clean platoon advantage make him the anchor of our production, while **Josh Lowe** benefits from a massive 14% platoon boost against the right-handed Civale. **Josh Jung** (64.09) is another critical cog in the lineup today, as he leverages a 14% park factor advantage and strong SP skill numbers against Kyle Freeland to secure a high-confidence start despite the platoon neutrality.\n\nWhile our lineup is set, we are monitoring the volatility of the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses, particularly for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (54.80) and **Gunnar Henderson** (50.28). Both face tough pitching\u2014Cam Schlittler and Matz\u2014and while their raw talent holds their floors steady, their scores are depressed by significant SP skill penalties (-12% and -2%, respectively). **Sam Antonacci** (59.55) remains a priority play despite a modest park factor; his elite xwOBA (0.402) and top-of-the-order positioning provide an essential ceiling that outweighs the risk of facing Emerson Hancock. The most difficult bench decision involved **Miguel Vargas** (50.46). He was the most viable alternative, but the optimizer ultimately prioritized the defensive versatility and higher-leverage lineup slotting of **Nolan Schanuel** (53.79). \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the SP matchups throughout the day. **Jackson Merrill** (49.48) faces the steepest climb, as he squares off against the elite arm of Shohei Ohtani; his score is buoyed only by a strong dynamic platoon advantage (+13%). Conversely, **Andy Pages** (61.67) provides sneaky value at the bottom of the order, and his involvement in our strategy is underscored by a conscious effort to capture SB upside where possible. With our bench anchored by **Dominic Smith** and **Coby Mayo**, we are prepared to pivot if official lineups significantly shift the projected order, though we are currently favoring the balance provided by our current starters.",
